[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Hi everyone. In this tutorial, we\'ll explain how to customize a character\'s voice in AI Studio. Although in previous tutorials, we showed that both Seaduns or Kling can'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'generate voices using prompts or references, using talking actor allows us to create more stable, emotionally rich voices at a much lower credit cost. &gt;&gt; The single alibi you gave me is a complete lie. You have two choices right'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'now. &gt;&gt; First, let\'s go over the talking actor with image workflow. After opening the talking actor interface, you can see that we can use either an image or a video as a reference.'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This means we can start from a single static image and use talking actor to generate both voice and body motion. So first, if we want to create a video for an influencer, we go to image create'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to generate an image. We select an AI actor as our main character, then describe the scene and actions in the prompt. Next, we choose realistic as the image style, and we can also adjust'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ratio and resolution. Finally, click generate. Once the image is ready, we go back to talking actor and drag the generated image into the interface as a reference. Then, in the text-to-voice panel, we can'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'generate the voice. First, under preset, we provide both male and female voice options. Below that, there are multiple character voices available to choose from. We can choose Aaron and click the play button'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to preview. &gt;&gt; Hi everyone. My name\'s Aaron. I\'m the fifth generation main actor for Reallusion Character Creator 5. &gt;&gt; Or Marco\'s voice. &gt;&gt; Look, the streets don\'t care about your plans. You either rule the concrete or'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you get crushed by it. &gt;&gt; And Octavio. &gt;&gt; Look, the streets don\'t care about your plans. You either rule the concrete or you get crushed by it.'

[01:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; In this case, I will choose Aaron\'s voice. Next, in the speech text field, we can enter the character\'s dialogue. You\'ll notice that the language is set to auto, which means the system will automatically detect the language and'

[02:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'generate the corresponding voice. After entering the dialogue, click generate voice. &gt;&gt; All right, so I\'ve been getting a ton of comments asking about Reallusion announces 2026 vision, so today we\'re finally diving into it.'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Once both the voice and dialogue are generated, we have to combine them with the reference image. At the bottom, we can describe the scene in the prompt and the character\'s actions. After finishing the prompt, click'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'generate to preview the final combined result. &gt;&gt; All right, so I\'ve been getting a ton of comments asking about Reallusion announces 2026 vision, so today we\'re finally diving into it.'

[02:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; We can also input different languages, such as German. Then, click generate voice. Or we can try Spanish as well.'

[03:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'With Talking Actor, we can quickly generate voices in different tones and'

[03:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'multiple languages and combine them with a single image. &gt;&gt; 2026 vision, so today we\'re finally'

[03:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'diving into it. &gt;&gt; Next, we can also use the reference audio. We can use a boy character from a fairy tale style. Since we cannot find a suitable voice in the preset list, we also support reference audio.'

[03:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You can import your own audio file. &gt;&gt; Do you ever feel like the world is moving a bit too fast? &gt;&gt; Then, enter the dialogue and click generate voice.'

[03:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Hey, you\'re late. I thought you guys weren\'t coming. &gt;&gt; After that, we again describe the scene and the character\'s actions in the prompt. Then click generate to see the final result.'

[04:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Hey, you\'re late. I thought you guys weren\'t coming. &gt;&gt; Finally, we can also use music or singing as a reference with audio to voice. First, we import an image as the'

[04:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reference as usual. Then switch to audio to voice and import the prepared music file. We describe the scene and character actions in the prompt again.'

[04:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then click generate to preview the result. Next, let\'s go over the video workflow. In iClone, the process of creating lip'

[04:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'sync animation or motion capture can be quite complex. So, we can use Talking Actor to quickly generate the character\'s voice and combine it with the original animation. First, we already have a prepared'

[04:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'character animation that we can preview. However, we have to change the visual style of this video. So, we go back to the first frame and click capture image to send it into 3D guided generation to create an image.'

[05:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Next, we select the model we want to use and adjust the aspect ratio and resolution. To improve character consistency, we can also add an AI actor. Here, we use Kevin.'

[05:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then in the prompt, we describe Kevin in the interrogation room, and we can describe the man\'s outfit into a detective style suit. After that, click generate to create the key image. Next, we go to 3D to video and click'

[05:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'capture video from 3D viewport to load the animation from iClone. Here, we choose Cidence as the generation model and adjust the aspect ratio and'

[05:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'resolution. We also add the same AI actor again to maintain character consistency. Finally, we describe the scene in the prompt and generate the video. At this point, we obtain a stylized'

[05:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video where the motion remains consistent with the original 3D environment. Next, we return to Talking Actor. We can now use the generated video as a reference input to generate voice.'

[06:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'First, we select Marco\'s voice. &gt;&gt; Look, the streets don\'t care about your plans. You either rule the concrete or you get crushed by it.'

[06:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Then input a dialogue related to an interrogation scene and click generate voice to preview the result. &gt;&gt; Every single alibi you gave me is a complete lie.'

[06:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You have two choices right now. You either look me in the eye and talk or you go down for all of it. &gt;&gt; Next, we describe the scene in the prompt and add facial expression guidance such as an angry expression.'

[06:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Then click generate. &gt;&gt; Every single alibi you gave me is a complete lie. You have two choices right now. You either look me in the eye and talk or'

[07:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you go down for all of it. &gt;&gt; However, we can observe that even though we specified an angry expression, the voice still sounds relatively calm. This happens because the generated voice itself is originally neutral and'

[07:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'emotional intensity cannot be fully controlled through prompt alone. So instead, we can enhance emotional control directly in the speech text field. We can use square brackets to describe structured emotion parameters in order:'

[07:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'emotion, tone, speaking speed, and voice style. After adding an angry emotional description, we can clearly hear that the voice becomes significantly more aggressive. &gt;&gt; Every single alibi you gave me is a'

[07:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'complete lie. Every single alibi you gave me is a complete lie. You have two choices right now. &gt;&gt; Next, we change the scene to a more relaxed, casual office environment. Here, we modify the speech text to a'

[07:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'happier line. &gt;&gt; Wow. We finally won first place. This is absolutely unbelievable. &gt;&gt; You may notice that the voice still sounds very low and unhappy.'

[08:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This happens because the emotional tone of the voice is also influenced by the reference voice\'s pitch and tone. To solve this, we switch to a more neutral-pitched reference voice.'

[08:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Hey there. Beautiful day, isn\'t it? &gt;&gt; After clicking generate again, you can clearly hear that the voice now feels much happier. &gt;&gt; Wow. We finally won first place. This is absolutely unbelievable.'

[08:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Finally, we make a few adjustments to the prompt description, and then we can successfully generate the video. &gt;&gt; Wow. We finally won first place. This is absolutely unbelievable. &gt;&gt; With the combination of 3D to talking'

[08:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'actor, we can quickly enhance facial expression and voice while maintaining motion consistency within a 3D environment. &gt;&gt; Look at this mess you made. YOU SCREWED UP THE WHOLE THING.'

[08:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; FOR more detailed speech text formats and emotional descriptors, please refer to the official manual, which includes full workflows and a variety of emotional control examples. Now that we\'ve covered single character'

[09:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'talking actor, let\'s move on to multiple talking actors. First, you\'ll need to provide either an image or a video as your reference. This feature supports two characters only, and it works best when the'

[09:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'characters are clearly placed on the left and right sides of the frame. This helps the AI recognize and separate them more accurately. Below, you\'ll see left voice and right voice, which represent the voices for each character.'

[09:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'For the left character, I\'m going to use Mila\'s voice. &gt;&gt; Seriously, you think that is going to stop me? You clearly haven\'t seen what I can do with &gt;&gt; For the right character, you can either'

[09:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pick another preset or load your own reference voice if you want a more specific sound. &gt;&gt; Seriously, you think that is going to stop me? &gt;&gt; [laughter] &gt;&gt; Next, let\'s build the conversation.'

[10:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Click add dialogue and a new speech segment will appear. Here, you can choose whether this dialogue is spoken by the left or right character, then simply type in the dialogue. Then click generate voice to'

[10:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'preview the result. &gt;&gt; All right, looks like everyone\'s here. Can the folks in the back see us? &gt;&gt; Once the text is entered, you\'ll see the length of that voice line automatically'

[10:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'generated. From there, you can keep adding dialogue segments. For example, we\'ll add another line for the left character. &gt;&gt; Wave your hands. We\'re taking a photo. &gt;&gt; Then another one for the right.'

[10:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Big smiles, everyone. &gt;&gt; And finally, end the conversation with the left character again.'

[10:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; All right, ready? 3 2 1 &gt;&gt; After everything is set, click preview dialogue to listen to the full conversation. &gt;&gt; All right, looks like everyone\'s here.'

[11:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Can the folks in the back see us? &gt;&gt; Wave your hands. We\'re taking a photo. &gt;&gt; Big smiles, everyone. &gt;&gt; All right, ready? 3 2 1 &gt;&gt; You might notice that the pacing feels a'

[11:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bit fast and compressed. To make it sound more natural, we can add pauses. Click add delay time. Set the duration you want. And drag the delay between the dialogue segments where you want the pause to'

[11:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'happen. Preview the dialogue again and you\'ll hear that the conversation now flows much more naturally and feels less rushed. &gt;&gt; Here. Can the folks in the back see us?'

[11:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Wave your hands. We\'re taking a photo. &gt;&gt; Big smiles, everyone. All right. Ready? 3 2 1. &gt;&gt; Finally, we describe the scene in the prompt. For example, we can say that the'

[11:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'audience is waving light sticks in the background and also describe each character\'s motion. Once that\'s done, just click generate and you\'ll get the final result. &gt;&gt; All right. Looks like everyone\'s here.'

[12:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Can the folks in the back see us? &gt;&gt; Wave your hands. We\'re taking a photo. &gt;&gt; Big smiles, everyone. All right. Ready? 3 2 1. &gt;&gt; Of course, all generated audio can be'

[12:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reused as a reference for other images or videos. By right clicking and selecting find file, you can locate the generated voice file, which is saved as a wave file and can be used independently.'

[12:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Finally, when returning to iClone, you can also apply the audio directly to a character in the 3D environment for use. By using images or videos as references'

[12:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with Talking Actor, you can quickly add customized voices to your characters. When combined with 3D to video, you can preserve the original 3D motion while enhancing the character with expressive'

[12:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'voice performance. Thanks for watching.'
